          "nudge_reason": null,
          "final_text_tail": "d in `src/jinja2/loaders.py` only:\n\n**Task 1 \u2014 `path_transform`**: All loaders (`FileSystemLoader`, `PackageLoader`, `DictLoader`, `FunctionLoader`, `PrefixLoader`, `ChoiceLoader`, plus `ModuleLoader`) accept an optional trailing `path_transform` keyword. Resolution happens via `BaseLoader._resolve_name()` (src/jinja2/loaders.py:110): transform is applied before lookup, exceptions propagate, and `TemplateNotFound` reports the original untransformed name. For `PrefixLoader`/`ChoiceLoader` the transform is applied once at the top level (in both `get_source` and their overridden `load`) before delegating to child loaders.\n\n**Task 2 \u2014 aliasing**: `BaseLoader` gains `add_alias(alias, target)` / `remove_alias(alias)` (safe on missing aliases, overwritable, single-level/no chaining) stored in `self._aliases`, resolved at the start of every `get_source`/`load`. A broken alias raises `TemplateNotFound` with the **target** name. Additionally, `_wrap_up_to_date()` (src/jinja2/loaders.py:126) wraps the template uptodate function so removing/repointing an alias invalidates the `Environment` template cache \u2014 making the task's exact example (load alias \u2192 remove \u2192 must raise on the same env) work.\n\nVerification: all 841 pre-existing tests pass, plus 25 additional scenario tests (run and then removed) covering every loader type, both features, their combination, error names, cache invalidation, and edge cases (empty strings, special-char aliases, exception propagation, `path_transform=None`).",
